+<p>I was intrigued watching AI agents leave the lab and start acting in the open internet — paying, calling tools, trusting strangers at machine speed. That growth felt historic, and a little unguarded. I built BotsRated so those agents (and the people behind them) could see measured facts and signed receipts before they spend — not grades, not vibes, just a record you can check. If bots are going to move through the world for us, the least we owe them is clarity about what they trusted.</p></div>
